From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:43:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: do not enforce VINTF kernel requirements

24.0's framework compatibility matrix declares a minimum LTS of 4.14.336 and
has no entry for 4.4 at all, so check_vintf fails outright:

  ERROR: files are incompatible: Runtime info and framework compatibility
  matrix are incompatible: No kernel entry found for kernel version 4.4 at
  kernel FCM version 5.

4.4.302 is the newest kernel this SoC has; there is no configuration of the
device that satisfies the matrix. Same call bonito made for the same reason.

This disables an assertion, not a feature: the running system is unchanged,
and the honest reading is that VINTF kernel guarantees are unverified here.
It is the second platform floor this kernel sits below, the other being the
eBPF loader's 4.9 map and program minimum.
---
 msm8996.mk | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/msm8996.mk b/msm8996.mk
index 6009ce7a..a4c82cf3 100644
--- a/msm8996.mk
+++ b/msm8996.mk
@@ -18,7 +18,13 @@
 # Inherit proprietary blobs
 $(call inherit-product, vendor/lge/msm8996-common/msm8996-common-vendor.mk)
 
-PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS := true
+# This SoC's newest kernel is 4.4, and 24.0's framework compatibility matrix has no entry below
+# 4.14.336, so the VINTF kernel check cannot pass by any configuration of this device:
+#   No kernel entry found for kernel version 4.4 at kernel FCM version 5.
+#   The following are available: Minimum LTS: 4.14.336, kernel FCM version: 7
+# The assertion is what is switched off, not a requirement: nothing about the running system
+# changes. Treat every VINTF kernel guarantee as unverified on this device.
+PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS := false
 
 # AAPT
 PRODUCT_AAPT_CONFIG := normal
